-- parse/bad: a comma list in a type is a PARAMETER list (language.md §3,
-- Types), so outside parentheses it has to be followed by `->`. Without one
-- there is nothing for the parameters to belong to, and the message is the
-- plain missing-token one rather than the tuple-element message, which
-- would name a reading these parentheses-free items never had.
x : Int, String
x =
    1
